{"id": "ev-59d70f625984", "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC33226/", "date": null, "coverage": "Loss of speciation rate will impoverish future diversity", "excerpt": "Human activities have greatly reduced the amount of the earth's area available to wild species. As the area they have left declines, so will their rates of speciation. This loss of speciation will occur for two reasons: species with larger geographical ranges speciate faster; and loss of area drives up extinction rates, thus reducing the number of species available for speciation. Theory predicts ", "limitation": "网页存档（curl），只用于所引数字/事实；日期为页面发布或检索所示日期，未注明者为 null", "local_archive": "data/sources/59d70f625984.json", "sha256": "2015ae1bbd0f498c4bb8f5fd4253dde41cbd700646b96932754094004dbde2fb", "verified": true}
