{"id": "ev-1d42897190ea", "url": "https://www.sciencefocus.com/space/humans-seeded-aliens-panspermia-2", "date": "2026-09-17", "coverage": "Scientists are now seriously asking if humans were seeded by aliens. Here’s why | BBC Science Focus Magazine", "excerpt": "In this scenario, life (or at least the ingredients for it) would have been delivered to Earth on comets or asteroids, seeding the planet with inhabitants – a process called panspermia. If it occurred, it could – and arguably should – have taken place on other planets too, perhaps suggesting alien life is common in the Universe, and maybe even hinting that we ourselves were originally aliens to th", "limitation": "网页存档（curl），只用于所引数字/事实；日期为页面发布或检索所示日期，未注明者为 null", "local_archive": "data/sources/1d42897190ea.json", "sha256": "22b464eb9b59887c296294f3d95b85ded749d5809df097571feac9284d3971c4", "verified": true}
