{"id": "ev-e918550a6103", "url": "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.infoandorg.2025.100582", "date": "2025-06-20", "coverage": "Homo agenticus in the age of agentic AI: Agency loops, power displacement, and the circulation of responsibility", "excerpt": "As attribution-making creatures, humans constantly seek to locate agency somewhere in their environment. Where we choose to attribute agency has profound consequences for our own sense of power, responsibility, and capacity to act. The rise of agentic AI systems disrupts these attribution processes, as humans encounter technologies that appear to act autonomously and control outcomes affecting hum", "limitation": "网页存档（exa-contents），只用于所引数字/事实；日期为页面发布或检索所示日期，未注明者为 null", "local_archive": "data/sources/e918550a6103.json", "sha256": "21b1dcef47afdab5ee6e159e6ce4c9feb83623100a0961036f3b95ab52aecdd8", "verified": true}
