{"id": "ev-31eb8b0a2d05", "url": "https://www.newscientist.com/article/1850470-its-life-but-not-as-we-know-it-2/", "date": "1998-07-03", "coverage": "It's life, but not as we know it | New Scientist", "excerpt": "Tom Ray, a “digital evolutionist” at Japan’s Advanced Telecommunications Research Institute, has since 1991 been running a software package called Tierra, a virtual world in which populations of simple computer programs breed and compete for resources. But none of these digital organisms has evolved into anything as complex as multicellular organisms. “Evolution in Tierra always led to stasis,” sa", "limitation": "网页存档（exa-contents），只用于所引数字/事实；日期为页面发布或检索所示日期，未注明者为 null", "local_archive": "data/sources/31eb8b0a2d05.json", "sha256": "5b4caacb68233cde201a18e400308114af4eb4cccd123058d78138e265d9e4dc", "verified": true}
