{"id": "ev-b7eebe383bf0", "url": "https://journals.sagepub.com/doi/10.1177/2053019619886670", "date": "2019-11-10", "coverage": "Deep-time organizations: Learning institutional longevity from history - Frederic Hanusch, Frank Biermann, 2020", "excerpt": "This study is a first attempt to pioneer the exploration of “deep-time organizations,” and to develop first hypotheses of what design features might allow societal and political organizations to survive and fulfill a mission over very long time. Given that such long-living organizations are rare, and that common social science methods such as experimentation or direct observation are impossible to", "limitation": "网页存档（exa-contents），只用于所引数字/事实；日期为页面发布或检索所示日期，未注明者为 null", "local_archive": "data/sources/b7eebe383bf0.json", "sha256": "716b4c676374056f75f0f13bb7f3aac9f6745591890534b4cd834773e0f200d5", "verified": true}
